A joint multi-result template whose results share an outer generic type,
(A[T], A[U]), with two consumers pinning different types, A[int] and A[bool]. The
two demands pin different slots of one instance, so plumb instantiates a single
Make[int, bool] producing both A[int] and A[bool], not two colliding instances.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type A[T any] struct{ V T }

//plumb:build
func Make[T, U any]() (A[T], A[U]) { return A[T]{}, A[U]{} }

//plumb:build
func UseInt(a A[int]) int { return 0 }

//plumb:build
func UseBool(a A[bool]) string { return "" }
